## Key Concepts

| Concept | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **Format string bug** | User input used directly as `printf` format string |
| **`%n`** | Writes bytes-printed-so-far into a pointer argument |
| **`%4$n`** | Positional — targets the 4th argument specifically |
| **Embedded address** | We put the target address in the input so it lands at position 4 |
| **Byte counting** | 4 (address) + 60 (`%60x`) = 64 = `0x40` — controls what `%n` writes |
| **Global variable** | Lives at a fixed address — not on the stack, not in libc — writable via `%n` |